      "writtenOn": "2024-12-04T17:10:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no /dev/kvm for this, hence we are introducing this new HAL. The details are available at go/pkvm-pvm-allow-vendor-tz-services-access, but here is tl;dr;:\n\nif vendor wants to issue their vendor-defined smcs (that should be in the vendor smc namespace, @willdeacon please chime in if i\u0027m saying nonsense here), then they need to:\n\n1. provide their EL2 module which will responsible for answering following questions from core pkvm code: \"hey vendor module, does this vm allowed to use this smc from vendor namespace?\"\n2. provide el1 driver that their el0 HAL (interface defined here) talks to. the el1 driver will get a vm_fd, resolve it into kvm_vm object, and pass to the el2 module (again Will or Seb please chime)\n3. provide el0 hal implementing the interface defining here\n\nfor the VMs that request access to the tee_services (defined in the VirtualMachineRaw / VirtualMachineApp configs), virtmngr will:\n\n1. use libselinux to check if that VM is actually allowed to access the tee_services\n2. connect to this HAL and pass vm_fd + list of requested tee services to it.",
      "parentUuid": "4f016a11_fa9a0b49",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 61
      },
